# {{.ProjectName}}

Go API with Chi router inspired by sriniously/go-boilerplate.

## Requirements

- Go 1.22+

## Setup

1. Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in your database config
2. Run the project

## Run

```bash
go mod tidy
go run ./cmd/api
```

## Structure

```
├── cmd/api/               # Entry point and dependency wiring
├── internal/
│   ├── config/            # Environment-based configuration
│   ├── database/          # Database connection and migrations
│   ├── errs/              # HTTP error types and factories
│   ├── item/              # Item module (ports, service, handler)
│   ├── logger/            # Structured logging (zerolog)
│   ├── middleware/        # Global middleware (CORS, logger, recovery)
│   ├── router/            # Route definitions
│   ├── server/            # HTTP server setup and lifecycle
│   ├── sqlerr/            # PostgreSQL error classification
│   └── validation/        # Request binding and validation
└── pkg/meta/              # Pagination helper
```

## Endpoints

- `POST /api/v1/items`       — Create an item
- `GET  /api/v1/items/{id}`  — Get item by ID
